{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall send outside the camp</b> – After he erected the Tabernacle, He commanded concerning the sending forth of the impure persons from the camp, so that the camp would be holy and fit for the Shekhinah to dwell in it, and this is a commandment that applies immediately and for all generations. And because He counted Israel by their families, by their fathers' houses, and separated from them the mixed multitude that was among them, He completed with the guilt-offering of consecrated things the law of one who robs a convert."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:42.421131275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}